3 with law; that no procedural or jurisdictional error has been committed either of the Authorized Officer or appellate Authority, as well reasoned order was passed by the Authorized Officer which was upheld by the Appellate Authority; that this court cannot sit as appellate authority to decide the settled issue raised in earlier writ petition of the petitioners when conclusion arrived is based on sufficient and relevant material; that the petitioners have approached this court with unclean hands and have suppressed the material facts.
